# Squinder Project Conventions

## Platform

- Expo is web-first, while preserving iOS and Android support.
- Keep UI and business logic compatible with `react-native-web`.
- For native-only libraries, provide a web adapter or platform-specific file.
- Telegram Mini App will reuse Expo Web; isolate Telegram SDK integration behind a web-only adapter.

## Backend and data

- Use Fastify on Node.js 22 and keep compatibility with Railway.
- PostgreSQL 18 with pgvector is the primary database; access it through Drizzle ORM.
- Add schema changes as Drizzle migrations and verify them against the Docker database.
- Keep `/health`, WebSocket, and SSE operational when changing API infrastructure.
- Store session tokens only as hashes in PostgreSQL.

## Dependencies and scaffolding

- Initialize frameworks with their official generators.
- Prefer current package versions, but never override Expo SDK compatibility pins blindly.
- After changing Expo dependencies, run `expo-doctor` and TypeScript checks.
- Use Expo development builds for native SDK features; do not assume Expo Go compatibility.

## Local workflow

- Keep `make prep`, `make web`, `make ios`, and `make android` working.
- API and PostgreSQL run in Docker; Expo and device tooling run on the host.
- Verify user-facing flows on Expo Web in addition to static checks.

## AI

- Add Mastra agents only for genuinely agentic or model-driven flows.
- Keep deterministic forms, validation, persistence, and authentication outside agents.
